  "label": "audience description",
  "description": "The meme is designed for an audience familiar with or interested in debates around identity politics, particularly the perceived incompatibility between Islamic and LGBTQ+ identities. It targets individuals who may hold or be exposed to Islamophobic or anti-LGBTQ+ stereotypes, and who are likely to interpret the visual juxtaposition and text as commentary on cultural conflict or societal norms. The audience is expected to understand the symbolic weight of the niqab and rainbow flag, and to engage with the text's condescending framing, which implies a lack of agency or competence in the individuals depicted. This audience may include those who are politically or culturally aligned with conservative or reactionary viewpoints that frame these identities as mutually exclusive or problematic.",
